  <element>
    <id>Text</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>48</y>
      <w>1300</w>
      <h>26</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Primary actor on the left; supporting systems on the right. Feature IDs (F01-F13) under each use case show coverage; N01 and N02 were added in the implementation.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLActor</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>110</x>
      <y>640</y>
      <w>140</w>
      <h>130</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Meal Planner
(primary user)</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLActor</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1430</x>
      <y>330</y>
      <w>200</w>
      <h>130</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>«system»
OpenAI API
(Responses API,
structured output)</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLActor</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1430</x>
      <y>900</y>
      <w>200</w>
      <h>130</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>«data source»
Statistics Canada
retail prices</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>20</x>
      <y>1610</y>
      <w>425</w>
      <h>80</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>GUI and CLI are boundary components inside MealIQ,
not actors: both reach these use cases through the
same MealPlanningFacade (no duplicated business logic).
bg=#FFFDE7</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1150</x>
      <y>1610</y>
      <w>534</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Supporting actors never initiate a use case. The OpenAI API
proposes plans, recipes, and changes; MealIQ validates them
deterministically before anything is saved. Prices are packaged
Statistics Canada data; recipes come from the catalogue and AI.
bg=#FFFDE7</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLUseCase</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>600</x>
      <y>1322</y>
      <w>470</w>
      <h>76</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>N01  Ask the agent in plain language
(starts UC01-UC09 from one typed request)</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLUseCase</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>600</x>
      <y>1450</y>
      <w>470</w>
      <h>76</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>N02  Review the agent check-up
(Home page; proposes UC04, UC06, UC07, UC09)</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
